=== "Trace and Optimize" ===

AAO provides a "Trace and Optimize" component. Users can add it to the Avatar's root<ref name="component-trace-and-optimize">https://vpm.anatawa12.com/avatar-optimizer/en/docs/reference/trace-and-optimize/</ref>; typically, GameObject with the [[Avatar Descriptor]].

The documentation describes this design principle as follows<ref name="component-trace-and-optimize" />:

<blockquote>
Trace and Optimize is quite carefully designed under the premise that “never let it affect the appearance.”

So, if any problems occur, [...] they are all caused by bugs in AAO, without exception.
</blockquote>

This component automatically applies optimizations equivalent to those performed by the following components when it determines that they are safe.

=== Merge Skinned Mesh ===

This component ''manually'' merges Unity SkinnedMeshRenderer components<ref name="component-merge-skinned-mesh">https://vpm.anatawa12.com/avatar-optimizer/en/docs/reference/merge-skinned-mesh/</ref>.

This component is usually not required, as "Trace and Optimize" automatically performs the same optimization in most cases<ref name="component-merge-skinned-mesh" />:

<blockquote>
Trace and Optimize will automatically do the same process, so in most cases you do not need to use this component.
</blockquote>

=== Freeze Blendshape ===

This component ''manually'' freezes [[Community:Terminology#Shapekey|Blendshape]]s at once in their initial weight<ref name="component-freeze-blendshape">https://vpm.anatawa12.com/avatar-optimizer/en/docs/reference/freeze-blendshape/
</ref> and remove it from the mesh. It must be added to same GameObject as SkinnedMeshRenderer<ref name="component-freeze-blendshape" />.

By definition, it does not consider animations that affect blendshapes; if the blendshapes are animated, consider using [[Community:Modular Avatar|Modular Avatar]]'s "Mesh Cutter" component instead.

=== Remove Meshes by various selection ===

Following components remove parts of mesh by their input:
* [https://vpm.anatawa12.com/avatar-optimizer/en/docs/reference/remove-mesh-by-blendshape Remove Mesh By BlendShape] - uses Blendshapes
* [https://vpm.anatawa12.com/avatar-optimizer/en/docs/reference/remove-mesh-by-mask Remove Mesh By Mask] - uses a Texture
* [https://vpm.anatawa12.com/avatar-optimizer/en/docs/reference/remove-mesh-by-box Remove Mesh By Box] - uses cuboids
* [https://vpm.anatawa12.com/avatar-optimizer/en/docs/remove-mesh-by-uv-tile/ Remove Mesh By UV Tile] - uses [[Community:Poiyomi Shaders|"UV Discard"]]-compatible configuration.

By definition, it does not consider animations that affect blendshapes; if the blendshapes are animated, consider using [[Community:Modular Avatar|Modular Avatar]]'s "Mesh Cutter" component instead.

